  "summary": "Full assessment of all 243 French/Vietnamese passages in five parts and both titles. Félicité’s service, her lost fiancé, the children, Victor’s death, Virginie’s death, the parrot Loulou and the final Corpus Christi vision are complete, with Flaubert’s irony, lists and free indirect style intact. The separate-context pass scored 8.675 with no major findings and seventeen minor ones; the substantive fidelity, imagery, naturalness and punctuation issues were revised and two cosmetic items remain open. Fidelity, imagery and mechanics are 9.0, voice and naturalness 8.5. Unrounded weighted score 8.8 meets the unchanged 8.6 threshold. No unresolved major or critical issue remains.",
  "title_review": {
    "source_title": "Un cœur simple",
    "target_title": "Một tấm lòng chất phác",
    "rationale": "Một tấm lòng chất phác keeps cœur as the seat of love (tấm lòng) and simple as guileless, not plain; the assessor preferred it to Một tâm hồn chất phác, which clashed with âmes in the text."
  }
